-- title:
--   Strict ordinarity from non-flatness for modular mod p representations
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal) of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$ whose image lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$: a $k$-vector space $V$ of rank $2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho$ from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k V$ that is trivial on the automorphisms fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; assume $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible, i.e. its base change to an algebraic closure of $k$ is irreducible. Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals, $N \geq 1$ with $p \mid N$ and $p^2 \nmid N$, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$. Assume that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $\ell$ is a non-unit and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$ (lying in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$ and acting on the residue field of $P$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$), the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho.\rho\,\sigma$ is $X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Assume finally that the rank-two adic representation [`GaloisRepAdic.ofResidualGaloisRep`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L196) attached to $\bar\rho$ is not finite flat at $p$ in the sense of `IsFlatAt`: it is not the case that for every ideal $I$ of $k$ with $k/I$ finite the Galois module $V/IV$ arises, compatibly with the Galois action, as the group of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points of a finite flat cocommutative Hopf algebra over the subring of $\mathbb Q$ of rationals with denominator prime to $p$. Then that adic representation is strictly ordinary at $p$: the image of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $k$, and for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $p$ is a non-unit there is a submodule $L \subseteq V$ spanned by the first vector of some basis indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,2$, stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$, such that every element of the inertia subgroup of $P$ acts trivially on $V/L$, and such that each $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup acts on $L$ by a scalar $x$ and on $V/L$ by a scalar $z$ with $x - a z \in (p^n)$ whenever $\sigma$ raises all $p^n$-th roots of unity to the power $a$.
--
--   This is the assertion that a weight-two modular mod $p$ representation of odd residue characteristic, of level $N$ exactly divisible by $p$, which fails to be finite flat at $p$, carries an ordinary filtration at $p$ on which the decomposition group acts by the cyclotomic character times the unramified character of the quotient — the strict ordinarity hypothesis required by the multiplicity-one and lifting arguments in the $p \mid N$ case. It is used in the construction of the auxiliary-level Hecke modules and in the analysis of the local Hecke action of $U_q$ at squarefree level.
